    "evidence_text": "This new dataset complements ZuCo 1.0 by providing experiments designed to analyze the differences in cognitive processing between natural reading and annotation.\n\nThe data is freely available here: url{this https URL\n\nPhysiological data can be used to understand and improve the labelling process (e.g. tokunaga2017eye), and, for instance, to build cost models for active learning scenarios .\n\nwith models trained on physiological activity data recorded from humans while reading?\n\nMotivated by these questions and our previously released dataset, ZuCo 1.0 , we developed this new corpus, where we specifically aim to collect recordings during natural reading as well as during annotation.\n\nIt contains physiological data of each subject reading 739 English sentences from Wikipedia (see example in Figure FIGREF1).\n\nHowever, the main difference and reason for recording ZuCo 2.0, consists in the experiment procedure.\n\nThis, and extending the dataset with more sentences and more subjects, were the\n\nThe experiment was programmed in MATLAB 2016b , using PsychToolbox .\n\nThis is the first dataset that allows for the comparison between these two reading paradigms.\n\ndesign in detail and conducted an extensive validation to ensure the quality of the recorded data.",
